hadiths[90]{hadithnumber,text}:
"124","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir bin Zaid (may Allah be pleased with him) that he was asked about the times of prayers, so he said: Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: ""The time for the Fajr prayer is from the appearance of dawn until sunrise,"" then he mentioned the times for all the prayers. Then he said that Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) says: ""I performed eight rak‘ahs (the first prayer—Dhuhr—and ‘Asr) with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) in Madinah."" The narrator stated: Jabir bin Zaid was asked about the prayer of a traveler, so he said: Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) said that he traveled with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and Abu Bakr and ‘Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) from Madinah to Makkah; all of them, from the time they departed Madinah until they returned from Makkah, during the journey and while staying in Makkah, would perform two rak‘ahs (qasr prayer). And Sayyidah ‘Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to perform two rak‘ahs of prayer in Makkah before the migration; when he came to Madinah, four rak‘ahs were made obligatory upon him, and his prayer in Makkah (two rak‘ahs) was prescribed for the traveler."
"125","Abu Rafi’ narrated: I prayed the ‘Isha prayer behind Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), and he recited Surah Al-Inshiqaq and performed a prostration of recitation in it. I said: Abu Hurairah! What is this prostration? He replied: I performed this prostration behind Abu Al-Qasim (peace and blessings be upon him), so I will continue to perform this prostration until I meet him."
"126","Abu Rafi' narrates: I saw Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) perform a prostration in Surah Al-Inshiqaq, so I said to him: Do you perform a prostration in this (Surah)? He replied: I saw my beloved (the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him) perform a prostration in it, so I will continue to perform a prostration in it until I meet him."
"127","Shu’bah, may Allah have mercy on him, narrated with this same chain, he said: I said: The Prophet (ﷺ), he said: The Prophet (ﷺ)."
"128","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""When any one of you waits for prayer while sitting on his prayer place, he is considered to be in prayer, and the angels say: O Allah! Forgive him, have mercy on him, (this continues) until he gets up and leaves or commits a bad hadath."" It was asked: What is a bad hadath? He said: ""That he passes wind audibly or silently."
"129","Saeed bin Musayyib (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) a narration similar to the previous hadith."
"130","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""When any of you is in the state of prayer, he should neither spit in front of him nor to his right side, but under his left foot. If he cannot do so, and he did like this, he spat in his garment, then rubbed it."
"131","Qasim bin Mehran Al-Qaisi narrated, I heard Abu Rafi’ narrating from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""When any of you is in prayer, he should not spit in front of him nor to his right side, but should spit under his left foot. If he cannot do so, then he should spit on the edge of his garment and do like this,"" and he rubbed his garment."
"132","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""If any of you knew that when he prays with me, it is better for him than being called towards a fat, healthy goat or two fat, healthy goats, then he would surely do it (be present in the prayer). For what is in it is much greater for him."
"133","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Does any one of you not fear that if he raises his head before the Imam raises his head from prostration, Allah may turn his head into the head of a donkey or his appearance into the appearance of a donkey?"
"134","From another chain of narration, it is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) similar to the previous hadith, except that in this one he said: ""Allah will change his head."
"135","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Last night, a great jinn tried to distract me so that he could break my prayer, but Allah gave me control over him, so I pushed him away forcefully. I intended to catch him and tie him to one of the pillars of the mosque so that you all could see him in the morning."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Then I remembered the supplication of my brother Sulaiman (peace be upon him): 'My Lord! Forgive me and grant me a kingdom such as shall not belong to anyone after me.' So Allah sent him back in disgrace."
"136","From another chain of narration, a similar hadith is narrated from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him. And in place of «يفتك» , a similar word is mentioned."
"137","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to seek refuge from the punishment of Hell, the punishment of the grave, and the False Messiah (Dajjal)."
"138","Narrated by Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to raise his hands (so much) while supplicating that his armpits would become visible. He said: I think this was during the prayer for rain (Istisqa)."
"139","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Go outside and announce that there is no prayer without reciting Surah Al-Fatihah and something more (from the Qur'an)."
"140","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""The callers to prayer will have the longest necks on the Day of Resurrection."
"141","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""Wherever the voice of the muezzin reaches, he is forgiven up to that point; every wet and dry thing that hears him bears witness to him, and for the one who offers prayer in congregation after hearing the adhan, there are twenty-five good deeds."
"142","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: When the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) would say the opening takbeer in prayer, he would remain silent for a short while before beginning the recitation. I asked, ""O Messenger of Allah! May my parents be sacrificed for you! What is the silence you observe between the opening takbeer and the recitation?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) replied: ""I say: O Allah! Distance me from my sins as You have distanced the East from the West. O Allah! Purify me of my sins as a white garment is cleansed of dirt. O Allah! Wash away my sins with water, snow, and hail."
"143","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would remain silent for a brief moment when saying Allahu Akbar (the takbir). The narrator said, I asked Sufyan: At the time of the opening takbir of the prayer? He replied: Yes."
"144","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""Whoever leaves his house in a state of ablution heading towards the mosque in order to perform the obligatory duties of Allah, then with every step he takes, one of his sins is erased and with the other his rank is elevated."
"145","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: We halted during a journey with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) for the purpose of resting, and we slept until we felt the heat of the sun, then we woke up. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Each of you should move his mount from this place, for in this place you encountered the issue which you know about."" The narrator states: So we moved away from there. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) asked for water and performed ablution, then he and his noble companions (may Allah be pleased with them) prayed two rak‘ahs. Then the iqamah was given, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) led us in the Fajr prayer after the sun had risen."
"146","A man went out of the mosque, so Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) said: He has disobeyed Abul Qasim (peace be upon him)."
"147","Abu’l-Sha’tha’ narrated: After the call to prayer for Asr had been given, a man went out of the mosque, so Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: He has disobeyed Abu’l-Qasim (peace be upon him)."
"148","Ibrahim bin Al-Muhajir narrated from a man, from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), a narration similar to the previous hadith."
"149","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that he saw a man leaving the mosque after the call to prayer had been given. He said: He has disobeyed Abul Qasim (ﷺ). The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) commanded us: ""When the muezzin has given the call to prayer, do not leave (the mosque) until you have performed the prayer."
"150","Abu Al-Awbar narrated: I was with Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), when a man came to him and said: Have you forbidden people from praying in shoes? He replied: I have not forbidden it, but by the Lord of the Ka'bah! I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) behind Maqam Ibrahim wearing shoes, then he returned while still wearing shoes. A man said: Have you forbidden people from fasting on Friday? He replied: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Do not fast on Friday, for it is a day of Eid, unless you join it with other days."" The narrator said: Then he began to narrate the hadith, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was sitting outside while the people (the noble companions, may Allah be pleased with them) were sitting with him, when suddenly a wolf came until it sat in front of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), then it began to wag its tail. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This wolf is an envoy of the other wolves, do you give it anything from your wealth?"" They all said: No, by Allah! We will not give it anything. Then a man stood up and threw a stone at it, and it went back barking. He said: This is a wolf, and what is a wolf?"
"151","Ziyad al-Harithi narrated: I was with Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), when a man said to him: Have you forbidden people from praying while wearing shoes? So he mentioned the previous hadith with these words: ""Then you returned and you were wearing shoes,"" similar to the previous hadith, and he did not mention the words after that."
"152","Abu Al-Awbar narrated: I was with Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), when a man said to him: Have you forbidden people from praying while wearing shoes? Then the narrator mentioned the story about the shoes and the hadith regarding fasting on Friday, similar to the previous narration, and did not mention what comes after that."
"153","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, that he said: ""A man's prayer in congregation is twenty-five times more rewarding than his prayer alone."
"154","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""A man's prayer in congregation is twenty-five times more virtuous than his prayer alone."
"155","Abu Al-Ahwas narrated from Abdullah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), a narration similar to this."
"156","Ibn Abi Khalid narrated from his father, he said: I saw Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him), he performed the Fajr prayer and he would shorten it. I said: Abu Huraira! Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) use to pray like this? He said: Yes, even shorter than this."
"157","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""A dog, a donkey, and a woman (by passing in front of the one praying) break the prayer."
"158","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates marfu‘an that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When any one of you prays, he should pray facing something which he takes as a sutrah. If he does not find anything, he should draw a line. Then, whoever passes in front of him after that will not harm him."
"159","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""When the Imam says «ولا الضالين» and the 'Ameen' of the people of the earth coincides with the 'Ameen' of the inhabitants of the heavens, Allah forgives all the previous sins of the servant. And the example of the person who does not say 'Ameen' is like that of a man who went on a journey of jihad with some people, and they drew lots. Their share came out before his share, so he said: Why did my share not come out? He was told: You did not say 'Ameen'."" Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: It was the practice of the Imam that when he said «ولا الضالين» , he would say 'Ameen' in a loud voice."
"160","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""I intended to order for the prayer to be established, then for the call to prayer (iqamah) to be given, then to order some young men to gather bundles of wood, then to have them set fire to those who do not come to the prayer."
"161","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""I intended to order the young men to gather bundles of wood, then I would command for the prayer and the call to prayer would be given, then I would burn the houses of those who hear the call to prayer but do not come to perform the prayer."
"162","Fadl bin Musa and Al-Mala'i narrated with this chain in a similar manner."
"163","Syedna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: A blind man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: ""I have no guide to lead me to the prayer (in congregation)."" So he requested the Prophet to grant him permission to pray at home. The Prophet (peace be upon him) gave him permission. When he turned to leave, the Prophet (peace be upon him) called him back and said: ""Do you hear the call to prayer (adhan)?"" He replied: ""Yes."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""Then come for the prayer."
"164","Narrated by Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""A woman, a dog, and a donkey (passing in front of a praying person) break the prayer, while something like the rear end of a saddle protects it."
"165","Ata (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated: The last piece of wood of the saddle is equal to a hand. And Muammar narrated from Qatadah (may Allah have mercy on him): One hand and one span."
"166","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""May Allah curse the Jews and the Christians, they took the graves of their prophets (peace be upon them all) as places of worship."
"167","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""Allah says: I have divided the prayer between Myself and My servant into two halves, and for My servant is what he asks for. Half of it is for him and half is for Me. When the servant says: «الحمد لله رب العالمين» the Lord Almighty says: My servant has praised Me. When he says: «الرحمن الرحيم» the Lord says: My servant has extolled Me. When he says: «مالك يوم الدين» the Lord says: My servant has glorified Me. When he says: «اياك نعبد واياك نستعين» He says: This is for My servant, and for My servant is what he has asked for. When he says: «اهدنا الصراط المستقيم» then He says: This is for My servant, and for My servant is what he has asked for."" Al-Fadl narrated it in the same way."
"168","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""Whoever regularly observes the two rak'ahs of the Duha prayer, his sins will be forgiven even if they are as much as the foam of the sea."
"169","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""I am seeing nations who will be brought out of Hell in chains and taken towards Paradise."
"170","Abu Awn Al-A'war narrated: I prayed with Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), and he used to say Allahu Akbar every time he stood up and between the two prostrations. Then he would say: ""I am the one among all of you whose prayer most resembles the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and this was his prayer throughout his life."
"171","Ibn Aun narrated from Muhammad about the man who misses a part of his prayer, so Muhammad said: He will make it up at his stations. A man said: Like a debt? So he replied: A matter is like a matter, and it is even better than that."
"172","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""When the iqamah for prayer is given, then there is no other prayer except the obligatory prayer."
"173","With this same chain, the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""When any one of you performs an obligatory prayer and does not complete its bowing, prostration, takbir, and humility, then he is like a merchant whose wealth does not increase, to the extent that even his principal amount is not fulfilled."
"174","With this same chain, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The worst thief is the one who steals from his prayer."" It was asked: O Messenger of Allah! How does he steal from his prayer? He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""He does not complete its bowing nor its prostration."
"175","With this same chain, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""The straightening of the rows is part of the perfection of prayer."
"176","With this same chain, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Whoever prays our prayer, faces our qiblah, eats our slaughtered animals, and fasts in our (month of) Ramadan, then this person is a Muslim; for him is the protection of Allah and His Messenger."
"177","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""Whoever consistently observes the two rak‘ahs of the Duha prayer, his sins will be forgiven even if they are as much as the foam of the sea."
"178","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that my beloved (peace and blessings be upon him) advised me regarding three things which I will never leave throughout my life: about two rak'ahs of Duha prayer, fasting three days every month, and that I should sleep after performing Witr."
"179","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) advised me—I will not say that my close friend (intimate companion) advised me—the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) has already said: ""If I were to take a close friend from among the people of the earth..."" He (peace and blessings be upon him) advised me to fast three days every month, to pray two rak'ahs of Duha (forenoon prayer), and to sleep after offering Witr."
"180","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""The first thing for which a servant will be called to account is his prayer. If he has performed it completely, it is good; otherwise, Allah Almighty will say: Look, does My servant have any voluntary prayers? If his voluntary prayers are found, He will say: Complete his obligatory prayers with them."
"181","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""A person remains in prayer as long as he stays at his prayer place, and waiting for the prayer keeps him seated there. The angels who are with him say: O Allah! Forgive him, O Allah! Have mercy on him, and this continues as long as he remains in a state of ablution."
"182","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""In prayer, for men it is to say 'Subhan Allah' (to alert the imam in case of forgetfulness or mistake), and for women it is to clap. And whoever makes such a gesture in his prayer that is understood (by others), then he must repeat his prayer."" This is the last hadith narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"183","Lady Umm Farwah (may Allah be pleased with her), who was among those who pledged allegiance to the Noble Prophet (peace be upon him), narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) was asked: ""Which deed is the best?"" He (peace be upon him) replied: ""To perform the prayer at its earliest time."
"184","Lady Umm Ayub (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""The Qur'an has been revealed upon seven recitations; all of them are satisfactory and sufficient."
"185","Umm Habibah (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""Whoever prays twelve (emphasized) rak'ahs during the day, Allah will build a house for him in Paradise."
"186","It is narrated from Sayyida Umm Habibah (may Allah be pleased with her) that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) heard the muezzin, he would repeat the same words as he said."
"187","It is narrated from Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that Shurayh (may Allah have mercy on him) asked her about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him): She replied: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to pray Tahajjud as much as Allah willed for him to pray, then when the time for Fajr prayer came, before leading it, he would pray two rak‘ahs, then he would go and lead the Fajr prayer. Shurayh (may Allah have mercy on him) asked her: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would return to you from the mosque, what would he do? She replied: ""He would begin with the miswak (tooth-stick)."
"188","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would perform the Tahajjud prayer, he would begin the prayer with two light rak‘ahs."
"189","It is narrated from Sayyida Umm al-Husayn (may Allah be pleased with her), she prayed behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and I heard him say: «مالك يوم الدين» Then when he recited «ولا الضالين» , he said: ""Ameen"" so much so that I heard his voice while I was in the women's row."
"190","Sayyiduna Usama bin Zaid narrated: I asked Tawus during a journey about dhikr and voluntary prayers, while Hasan bin Muslim bin Yanaq was sitting. So Hasan said: Tawus narrated to me from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) prescribed the obligatory prayer for both residence and travel, and just as prayers are offered before and after it in residence, he said: In the same way, prayers will be offered before and after it during travel."
"191","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated: Your Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was commanded to prostrate on seven bones, and that neither hair nor clothes should be gathered. Amr (bin Dinar) once narrated it as follows: The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I have been commanded to prostrate on seven bones, and I have been commanded not to gather the hair or the clothes."
"192","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated that the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) was commanded to prostrate on seven bones and not to gather his hair or clothes."
"193","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated: The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was commanded to prostrate on seven parts of the body, and not to gather the hair or clothes. Ibrahim bin Maisarah narrated: I asked Tawus (may Allah have mercy on him) about prostrating on the nose, and he said: It is better. Ishaq (may Allah have mercy on him) said: The forehead and the nose are the same thing."
"194","Tawoos (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates: We asked Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) about sitting with the buttocks placed on the feet between the prostrations. He replied: That is Sunnah. We said: When a person does this (sits like this), do you consider it good? He replied: Why not, it is the Sunnah of your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"195","Syedna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to teach us the Tashahhud in the same manner as he used to teach us a surah of the Qur'an."
"196","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Whoever catches one rak'ah of the Asr prayer before sunset has caught that (Asr) prayer, and whoever catches one rak'ah of the Fajr prayer before sunrise and one rak'ah after the sun has risen, he has caught that (Fajr) prayer."
"197","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated: The iqamah for prayer was given, but I had not yet performed the two rak‘ahs (Sunnah) before the Fajr prayer (after the salam), so I stood up and began to pray them. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) passed by me and said: ""Will you pray four rak‘ahs for the Fajr prayer?"" Salih (the narrator) was asked: Who said this? He replied: The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) did."
"198","It is narrated from Ibn Abi Mulaykah that the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said to a man: Then the narrator mentioned it similar to the previous hadith."
"199","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: ""We used to recognize the conclusion of the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) by the sound of 'Allahu Akbar'."
"200","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated: I stood up and began to pray two rak‘ahs while the iqamah for the (obligatory) prayer had been given. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Will you pray four rak‘ahs for the Fajr prayer?"
"201","Syedna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) prescribed four rak'ahs for the prayer at home, two rak'ahs for the prayer during travel, and one rak'ah for the prayer during fear."
"202","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated: Allah has, through the tongue of your Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), made obligatory the prayer of residence as four rak‘ahs, the prayer of travel as two rak‘ahs, and the prayer of fear as one rak‘ah."
"203","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever gives the call to prayer (adhan) for seven years seeking reward for the sake of Allah, freedom from Hell will be written for him."
"204","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Sa’d bin Abi Waqqas (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: To have the ability to call the adhan with the intention of reward for the sake of Allah’s pleasure is more beloved to me than jihad, Hajj, and ‘Umrah."
"205","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) delayed the ‘Isha prayer one night, so Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) called out to him: (O Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him) the prayer, the women and children have fallen asleep. So he came out while drops of water were falling from his head, and he (peace and blessings be upon him) was saying: “This is the (proper) time (for ‘Isha prayer), if I did not consider it difficult for my ummah.”"
"206","Ibn Jurayj narrated: I said to Ata’ (may Allah have mercy on him): At what time do you prefer the Imam and an individual to pray the ‘Isha prayer? He said: I heard Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) say: One night, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) delayed the ‘Isha prayer until the people fell asleep, then woke up, then fell asleep again, then woke up, then fell asleep again. Then Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) stood up and said: Prayer, prayer! The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came out. Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: It is as if I am looking at him, and drops of water were falling from his head, and he had placed his blessed hand on his head and was saying: “If I did not consider it difficult for my Ummah, I would have commanded them to pray at this (late) time.”"
"207","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) combined and performed Zuhr and Asr, and Maghrib and Isha prayers together during residence and travel."
"208","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated: Whoever from the Ummah of Muhammad sends Salat or Salam upon Muhammad (peace be upon him), it reaches him: so-and-so sends Salat upon you, and so-and-so sends Salam upon you."
"209","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever eats from these foul-smelling vegetables (such as garlic, onion, and radish, etc.), then he should not come near our mosques, because that which causes discomfort to humans also causes discomfort to the angels."
"210","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Garlic was not found in our area, rather there was onion and gindana (a type of vegetable), so we were prohibited from it."
"211","It is narrated from Hazrat Ata (may Allah have mercy on him) that he ate radishes so that he could make her smell its odor."
"212","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to pray on a mat made of palm leaves."
"213","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) praying in a single garment, using its extra part to protect himself from the heat and cold of the ground."
